  "notes": ["Exact original set0202 side construction and declared-zero-HP break run through visit 600. Sasuke uses declared rigid joints and actual collision to acquire the rebound plane or box. Stage bounds and phase are declared; the full retail arena is not loaded.","The active normal caller runs to its actor dispatcher. Group 40 has advanced the local rise offset while previous and current world roots remain equal. An independent carry-prefix probe on that state admits carry but does not lift Sasuke. The normal actor dispatcher is not resumed.","The alternate original updater does not call the actor updater. It runs group 40, stage/world, counter, shape publication and collision. On its first rise the allocated center holds and fresh contact stores a lower local anchor against the raised matrix, keeping the actor at the old height.","On the second rise the allocated center catches up. The retained-support actor moves up in collision even at the old pose. A fresh actor at identical current and previous sphere Y reaches the same narrow kernel but acquires no support; the fresh near-top control does acquire it.","Supported visits reach the original model-refresh boundary with the same Y as an isolated landing probe. No landing helper execution is inferred from a missing observation or an unchanged root. Unsupported visits stop before actor presentation and do not exercise the absent-support floor fallback.","No normal frame continuation, model refresh, physical control, full battle scheduling, original terrain, hardware or native gameplay is qualified."],
